1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:05,694
Lesson 3.3.4: Trending of Labs and Vitals.

2
00:00:09,800 --> 00:00:13,788
Trending means comparing the most recent value with the previous one,

3
00:00:13,828 --> 00:00:17,853
and saying whether it's improving, stable or worsening.

4
00:00:17,903 --> 00:00:21,615
For labs, that's every lab relevant to the CCM condition,

5
00:00:21,655 --> 00:00:25,239
plus hemoglobin A1C, from the past year.

6
00:00:25,289 --> 00:00:29,764
For vitals, it's blood pressure and weight, which we track for every patient.

7
00:00:29,814 --> 00:00:36,262
And some conditions add vitals of their own, like oxygen saturation for COPD.

8
00:00:38,567 --> 00:00:41,735
Every condition has its own monitoring criteria,

9
00:00:41,775 --> 00:00:44,394
and the Update Care Policy lists them.

10
00:00:46,333 --> 00:00:50,252
Its Numbers To Track tab shows what to monitor for each condition,

11
00:00:50,292 --> 00:00:51,720
and how often.

12
00:00:55,133 --> 00:00:57,946
For hyperlipidemia, that's the lipid profile,

13
00:00:57,986 --> 00:01:01,831
every 180 days, and blood pressure, every day.

14
00:01:04,533 --> 00:01:07,588
Blood pressure isn't a lab, so for trending of labs,

15
00:01:07,628 --> 00:01:10,172
the lipid profile is what we're after.

16
00:01:13,033 --> 00:01:17,032
PointClickCare keeps labs in three places: the Results tab,

17
00:01:17,072 --> 00:01:21,324
the Misc tab, and, as a last resort, the progress notes.

18
00:01:23,467 --> 00:01:25,036
The Results tab comes first.

19
00:01:25,076 --> 00:01:29,482
It's split into two sections, Laboratory and Radiology.

20
00:01:33,267 --> 00:01:40,292
Searching for lipid finds a single lipid panel, completed on July 15, 2026.

21
00:01:43,915 --> 00:01:47,158
Actions, then View Results, opens the report.

22
00:01:49,333 --> 00:01:58,947
Here's the lipid panel: cholesterol 100, triglycerides 143, HDL 44, and LDL 27.

23
00:02:03,267 --> 00:02:07,651
All four were collected on July 15, 2026.

24
00:02:10,133 --> 00:02:18,616
In the note, each lab gets its value and its date: HDL was 44 on July 15, 2026.

25
00:02:20,200 --> 00:02:25,011
Then comes the trend: the most recent value compared with the previous one.

26
00:02:26,667 --> 00:02:28,381
This panel was never repeated,

27
00:02:28,421 --> 00:02:32,016
so the note says there's no previous result to compare with.

28
00:02:32,967 --> 00:02:35,928
We also say whether the lab is controlled, improving,

29
00:02:35,968 --> 00:02:41,119
stable or worsening. Every value here is in the normal range.

30
00:02:44,900 --> 00:02:49,434
Triglycerides, total cholesterol and LDL follow the same pattern,

31
00:02:49,474 --> 00:02:51,530
all from the same date.

32
00:02:52,467 --> 00:02:55,790
With an earlier result, the note trends the two instead.

33
00:02:57,467 --> 00:03:03,454
Say HDL had been 29 in February 2026, below the normal range.

34
00:03:03,494 --> 00:03:08,491
Now it's 44, so the note says: improving, now controlled.

35
00:03:09,633 --> 00:03:14,134
And a lab we need but can't find at all is simply marked: not found.

36
00:03:16,867 --> 00:03:18,991
Three numbers are tracked for every patient,

37
00:03:19,031 --> 00:03:24,195
whatever the condition: blood pressure, weight, and hemoglobin A1C.

38
00:03:25,133 --> 00:03:29,945
A1C is the only lab of the three, so it belongs in this section too.

39
00:03:35,333 --> 00:03:41,059
Its report shows an A1C of 6, on August 19, 2026.

40
00:03:44,300 --> 00:03:51,589
So the note reads: hemoglobin A1C was 6.0 on August 19, 2026.

41
00:03:54,333 --> 00:03:59,853
And when there's no A1C at all, the note says so: not found, no recent A1C.

42
00:04:01,540 --> 00:04:04,170
Opening every report one by one takes time.

43
00:04:04,210 --> 00:04:09,131
The Trending button shows every value of a lab side by side.

44
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:15,210
Here we pick HDL and TSH, and search.

45
00:04:17,600 --> 00:04:23,532
HDL was measured once: 44, on July 15. That's what we already found.

46
00:04:26,433 --> 00:04:31,013
TSH has three values: 0.72 on November 9,

47
00:04:31,053 --> 00:04:37,702
0.42 on October 5, and 0.02 on August 19.

48
00:04:43,800 --> 00:04:46,738
If the Results tab comes up empty, the Misc tab,

49
00:04:46,778 --> 00:04:49,684
sometimes called Documents, is next.

50
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:55,545
It holds the patient's files,

51
00:04:55,585 --> 00:05:00,128
uploaded as PDFs instead of being entered in their own sections.

52
00:05:04,433 --> 00:05:06,209
Sorting by category groups them,

53
00:05:06,249 --> 00:05:10,050
and the Laboratory category holds the lab results.

54
00:05:12,767 --> 00:05:18,072
Each file opens a lab report, such as a metabolic panel or a CBC.

55
00:05:20,667 --> 00:05:24,878
The last resort is the progress notes, with View All, as before.

56
00:05:28,667 --> 00:05:31,692
This time the custom date range covers a whole year,

57
00:05:31,732 --> 00:05:36,000
because a lab from three, four or six months ago still counts.

58
00:05:40,867 --> 00:05:47,121
Here, the effective date runs from November 17, 2025 until today.

59
00:05:50,000 --> 00:05:53,025
Searching for HDL finds the same result:

60
00:05:53,065 --> 00:05:59,477
high density lipoprotein, 44, on July 15, 2026.

61
00:06:05,567 --> 00:06:10,014
So, the rules for labs: we document every lab relevant to the condition,

62
00:06:10,054 --> 00:06:12,785
plus A1C, from the past year.

63
00:06:12,835 --> 00:06:15,666
We look in the Results tab and the Misc tab first,

64
00:06:15,706 --> 00:06:19,378
and in the progress notes only if those two have nothing.

65
00:06:19,433 --> 00:06:22,904
The most recent result is trended against the previous one,

66
00:06:22,944 --> 00:06:25,373
and both must fall within that year.

67
00:06:25,433 --> 00:06:28,591
A result older than one year isn't documented.

68
00:06:30,967 --> 00:06:33,039
Trending of vitals works the same way,

69
00:06:33,079 --> 00:06:37,630
for the two vitals tracked for every patient: blood pressure and weight.

70
00:06:39,767 --> 00:06:41,660
The Weights and Vitals tab lists them,

71
00:06:41,700 --> 00:06:45,253
along with temperature, pulse and respiration.

72
00:06:46,900 --> 00:06:54,232
The most recent blood pressure is 132 over 70, on November 12, 2026.

73
00:06:56,933 --> 00:06:59,348
We compare it with a reading from the previous month:

74
00:06:59,388 --> 00:07:03,980
166 over 84, on October 20.

75
00:07:07,967 --> 00:07:12,756
That earlier reading was above our upper limit of 140 over 90,

76
00:07:12,796 --> 00:07:14,388
so it was uncontrolled.

77
00:07:16,000 --> 00:07:19,428
Now it's within range, so the note says: improving.

78
00:07:22,800 --> 00:07:26,610
Weight is next. View All beside it shows the weight history.

79
00:07:30,400 --> 00:07:37,711
The most recent weight is 191.7 pounds, on November 1, 2026.

80
00:07:37,767 --> 00:07:42,138
A month earlier, on October 4, it was 190.1 pounds:

81
00:07:42,178 --> 00:07:45,382
almost no change, so the weight is stable.

82
00:07:49,300 --> 00:07:52,239
The last section, vitals related to the condition,

83
00:07:52,279 --> 00:07:55,126
also comes from the outline of care.

84
00:07:57,300 --> 00:08:00,603
For hyperlipidemia, there's nothing beyond blood pressure,

85
00:08:00,643 --> 00:08:03,134
which we already track for everyone.

86
00:08:06,933 --> 00:08:10,945
So the note simply says: no vitals related to the condition.

87
00:08:12,800 --> 00:08:17,408
With COPD, though, the outline lists oxygen saturation.

88
00:08:18,533 --> 00:08:21,946
Then the most recent oxygen saturation would go here,

89
00:08:21,986 --> 00:08:26,434
trended against the previous reading, just like blood pressure and weight.

90
00:08:30,500 --> 00:08:34,334
To wrap up: the numbers to track come from the Update Care Policy,

91
00:08:34,374 --> 00:08:36,393
here the lipid profile.

92
00:08:36,443 --> 00:08:40,674
The Results tab comes first, through View Results or the Trending view.

93
00:08:40,724 --> 00:08:45,250
Then the Misc tab, and finally a one-year search of the progress notes.

94
00:08:45,300 --> 00:08:50,159
Each lab is trended, latest against previous, both within the past year.

95
00:08:50,209 --> 00:08:53,492
Blood pressure and weight are trended against the previous month,

96
00:08:53,532 --> 00:08:55,069
for every patient.

97
00:08:55,119 --> 00:08:59,214
And vitals related to the condition come from the outline of care.

98
00:09:01,367 --> 00:09:07,729
Still ahead in the problem note: gaps in care, symptoms, risk factors and complications, falls,

99
00:09:07,769 --> 00:09:15,689
provider visits, hospitalizations and ER visits, referrals, medication changes, and escalation.
